	// NOTE ON LAYOUT:
	// We choose layouts to improve cache locality of the kernel:
	//   * C, B: dims (j, i)  -> elements with consecutive i at fixed j are contiguous.
	//     In the computation we iterate j (outer) and i (inner), and we repeatedly
	//     access C[k,j] and B[k,j] varying k (i-dimension), so this makes both
	//     B[k,j] and C[k,j] contiguous in memory.
